  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Botanical Label",
    "overview": "The front desk reads like a fresh local product label: pandan green, calamansi yellow-green, coconut white, amber. It is a working tool first. White panels sit on a pale green-white ground, separated by thin hairlines instead of shadows, and colour appears only where it does a job: the rail you navigate with, the one action you take, the booking you are looking at, the category of a service, the state of an appointment. It must not read as a purple-on-grey admin template, nor as a cream-and-serif \"luxury\" page, and it must never be dark or heavy.\n\nThe theme is re-skinned per prospect. Every value below is the current Lumière skin, set in `src/config/spa.config.js` and pushed into CSS variables (`--brand-*`) by `applyTheme`; `src/index.css` maps those into Tailwind tokens (`bg-rail`, `text-ink`, `border-line`, ...). The roles are the system; the hex values are one skin. A new skin changes the values, never the roles.\n\nDensity is medium: 44px tap targets everywhere, 13–15px working text, tabular figures for every number a spa owner would compare.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Green side rail on desktop, green top bar plus white bottom nav on phones.",
      "Flat white panels with 1px hairlines; shadow only on things that float.",
      "One family (Figtree) at several weights; tabular numbers.",
      "Amber is the single primary action, always with ink text.",
      "Status is shown by words and shape, colour only reinforces it."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Roles Not Hex Rule",
        "body": "Components never hard-code a colour. They use the role tokens (`bg-rail`, `text-ink`, `border-line`, `bg-cat-*`) or `var(--color-*)` / `var(--brand-*)` inside arbitrary values, so a prospect's re-skin in `spa.config.js` reaches every pixel.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Guarded Pairs Rule",
        "body": "`src/config/themeContrast.test.js` asserts 4.5:1 for every text-on-ground pair the UI uses: ink on page, surface, accent, highlight and soft; muted on page and surface; rail-ink on rail and rail-active; accent-ink on surface and page; warn-ink on warn-bg; success on success-bg; danger on surface. A new skin must pass it, and a new text-on-colour pairing gets added to it.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ink On Bright Rule",
        "body": "Text on amber or calamansi is ink, never white.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Eleven Floor Rule",
        "body": "Nothing is set below 11px.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Figures Rule",
        "body": "Every money amount, count, time and date that sits in a column, tile or total uses tabular numbers.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hairline Not Shadow Rule",
        "body": "Panels, cards and tables separate with a 1px line border, never a resting shadow.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** take every colour from a role token or `var(--color-*)`; add any new text-on-colour pair to `themeContrast.test.js`.",
      "**Do** put ink text on amber and calamansi.",
      "**Do** keep panels flat: surface, 1px line border, 8px corners.",
      "**Do** make every tap target at least 44px.",
      "**Do** use tabular numbers for money, counts, times and dates.",
      "**Do** keep cancelled and no-show appointments visible as stamps.",
      "**Do** pair every colour signal with words, a shape or an icon: status label or icon, category name beside its band."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** hard-code hex values in components.",
      "**Don't** put white text on amber or calamansi.",
      "**Don't** put coloured side-stripe borders on cards or panels; the 4px category band inside an appointment row or block is the only left-edge colour, and it is data.",
      "**Don't** put eyebrow labels or kickers above headings.",
      "**Don't** let colour be the only signal of a state or category.",
      "**Don't** add a second type family or set text below 11px.",
      "**Don't** give resting panels a shadow, or turn the page ground beige."
    ]
